ReBIOS
======

ReBIOS is an EFI application that brings legacy BIOS booting back to UEFI-only
(class 3) systems. It is a minimal virtualisation layer, using Intel VMX or
AMD SVM, that runs SeaBIOS and the legacy operating system it boots on the
real hardware, passing as much as possible through to them unchanged. It is
meant as a drop-in replacement for CSMWrap.

Building requires a GCC or Clang toolchain and "git", used to fetch the
dependencies (see get-deps). SeaBIOS, which ReBIOS carries, additionally
requires GCC, GNU binutils, and "python3". "curl" is used to download the
EDK2 OVMF firmware images for "make run".

    ./get-deps
    make

Assembly files with the *.S extension are built using the same toolchain as
the C sources. Only *.asm files, of which ReBIOS ships none, require
"nasm".

The "TOOLCHAIN" and "TOOLCHAIN_PREFIX" make variables can be used to set
the toolchain. "TOOLCHAIN" can be set to "llvm" to use Clang/LLVM.
For example:
    make TOOLCHAIN=llvm
or:
    make TOOLCHAIN_PREFIX=x86_64-elf-

The program is linked through the compiler driver, using its default linker
for GCC and LLD for Clang. A different linker can be picked by adding a
"-fuse-ld=" option to "LDFLAGS".

Link-time optimisation can be enabled by adding "-flto" to "CFLAGS":
    make CFLAGS='-g -O2 -pipe -flto'

SeaBIOS is built with the GNU tools named by "SEABIOS_TOOLCHAIN_PREFIX",
which follows "TOOLCHAIN_PREFIX" but is empty for the "llvm" toolchain, or by
"SEABIOS_CC", "SEABIOS_LD", "SEABIOS_OBJCOPY", "SEABIOS_OBJDUMP", and
"SEABIOS_STRIP" individually. "HOST_CC" builds its configuration tools.

The video BIOS is built likewise, with the GNU tools named by
"VGABIOS_TOOLCHAIN_PREFIX", or by "VGABIOS_CC" and "VGABIOS_OBJCOPY", and with
the flags "VGABIOS_CFLAGS" (by default -g -O2 -pipe), "VGABIOS_CPPFLAGS", and
"VGABIOS_LDFLAGS" rather than "CFLAGS", "CPPFLAGS", and "LDFLAGS". It is always
built with -Os, as it has to fit in 32 KiB.

